# 4. Viewing Data

Large datasets can contain thousands of rows.

We normally do not print the complete dataset.

## head()

`head()` displays the first 5 rows.

```python
print(df.head())
```

To display the first 3 rows:

```python
print(df.head(3))
```

---

## tail()

`tail()` displays the last 5 rows.

```python
print(df.tail())
```

To display the last 2 rows:

```python
print(df.tail(2))
```

So:

```
head() → First rows

tail() → Last rows
```

